  "liner": {
   "body_md": "This recording captures the first of three consecutive shows at the Swedish American Hall in early 2020 [1][2]. The recommended file, tmg2020-02-20.matrix, offers a complete 19-song set lasting 82 minutes, utilizing a matrix mix that blends the soundboard with audience microphones for a balanced perspective [1]. The lineup begins with “Alpha Omega” and “Hand of Death,” the latter being a mythic rarity with only two archived performances [1]. It moves through “Running Away With What Freud Said” and “Tallahassee,” before featuring “Going to Cleveland,” a bustout that had not appeared in the archive for over two years [1]. The set includes “Rescue Breathing,” which is the first appearance of that song in the archive, alongside “You or Your Memory” and “The Best Ever Death Metal Band in Denton” [1]. Later tracks include “Wild Sage,” “New Star Song,” and “Slow West Vultures,” both of which are bustouts from previous months [1]. “You’re in Maya” and “Onions” follow, leading to “Sax Rohmer #1” and “Alpha Incipiens,” the latter being a bustout from nearly nine years prior [1]. The encore consists of “This Year,” “Golden Boy,” and “Attention All Pickpockets” [1]. This performance is the 302nd in the archive’s collection for the band, following a show at the Haw River Ballroom in December 2019 [3]. The recording was taped by Anonymouse and LMGBTapes, with the transfer handled by LMGBTapes [1].",
